{
  "Plan: The GRKN – shared meal-planning app for two": [
    "App name is The GRKN.",
    "The GRKN is used in the manifest, page titles, home-screen icon label (\"GRKN\"), invite emails, and push notifications."
  ],
  "Context": [
    "The app addresses the problem of partners deciding what to cook each week.",
    "The app addresses the problem of struggling to find new recipes that are good and nutritious for cooking each week."
    ],
  "Decisions (confirmed)": [
    "Backend and sync is Convex.",
    "Every query updates live on both phones with Convex."
    ],
    "iPhone-first UI rules (built in from day one, never added later)": [
      "Screen fit opens full screen from the home screen using standard iOS home-screen app settings.",
      "Content avoids the notch and home bar using viewport-fit=cover.",
      "Layout uses the dynamic viewport height so the Safari toolbar never cuts off content.",
      "Background bounce is locked so pull-to-refresh cannot fight with scrolling."
    ]
  }

{
  "Getting sync right (why this won't repeat the Firebase problem)": [
    "Each shopping item is its own document.",
    "Ticks set a value; they don't flip it. The tick action is `setChecked(itemId, checked: boolean)`, not \"toggle\". If you both tap the same item, the result is still correct and stable. Instant feedback: every tick, add and reorder shows on screen immediately and then syncs. Server-side list building: combining the week's recipes into a shopping list happens in one transactional step on the server. Rebuilding the list keeps ticked items, manual items and edits, and only adds, removes or adjusts the items that came from recipes. Connection indicator: a small dot shows \"Live / Reconnecting / Offline – changes will sync\". Changes made while offline are held and sent when you reconnect. In the store: the shopping screen keeps the phone awake, ticked items drop to the bottom of their aisle, and each tick shows who made it (\"✓ by Rory\")."
  ],
  "Data model (`convex/schema.ts`)": [
    "The `households` document has fields: `name`, `glutenFreeDefault`, `region/country` (for what's in season), `units` (metric), and `defaultServings).",
    "The `members` document has fields: `householdId`, `userId`, `displayName`, and `glutenFree` (boolean).",
    "The `invites` document has fields: `householdId`, `code`, and `expiresAt`. The `recipes` document has fields: `householdId`, `title`, `description`, `servings`, `prepMin`, `cookMin`, `tags[]`, `cuisine`, `source` (with kind: generated|url|instagram|photo|manual, url?), `glutenFree`, `glutenNotes?`, `ingredients[]` (with id, qty, unit, name, canonical, aisle, note?, optional?, glutenRisk, gfSwap?), `steps[]` (with id, text, timers[] {label, seconds}, ingredientIds[]), and `nutritionPerServing` (with kcal, protein, carbs, fat, fibre).",
    "The `ratings` document has fields: `recipeId`, `userId`, `stars` (1–5), `wouldCookAgain`, `comment?`, and `cookedAt`. The `tasteProfile` document has fields: `likes[]` and `dislikes[]` (ingredients or cuisines), `spiceLevel`, `notes`, and `summary`. The `summary` is rewritten by Claude from ratings, comments and dislikes every few ratings and is included in every generation prompt. The `pantry` document has fields: `householdId`, `name`, `canonical`, `qty?`, `unit?`, `useSoon` (boolean), and `addedAt). Ticking a shopping item can move it into the pantry (optional). \"Mark recipe cooked\" offers to remove the pantry items it used up."
  ]
}

{
  "Claude integration (`convex/ai.ts`, a Node server function)": [
    "The Claude integration uses the `@anthropic-ai/sdk` with structured output for valid, typed recipes.",
